## Verified by running code

### Declared coalition support

The pilot calls `_catalogue_with_census`, submits the catalogue to `evaluate_many`, and excludes invalid configurations before scoring at [run_v025_pilot_c3.py:740](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-coalgen-ws/scripts/run_v025_pilot_c3.py:740). The catalogue declares top-8 live legal unilateral options, top-two S0 proposals, top-10-user/top-two pairwise proposals, beam evacuations, explicit null handling, and a 1,500-row cap at [run_v025_matrix_probe.py:194](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-coalgen-ws/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/probe/run_v025_matrix_probe.py:194).

The implemented construction was read directly from the engine:

- complete Cartesian support is used only below the declared limit; otherwise every shortlisted unilateral is included ([lines 543–587](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-coalgen-ws/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/probe/run_v025_matrix_probe.py:543));
- users are ranked by their best exact nominal unilateral surplus ([lines 589–622](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-coalgen-ws/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/probe/run_v025_matrix_probe.py:589));
- the two S0 profiles, top-10-user/top-two pairwise combinations, and per-active-beam evacuations are added ([lines 624–654](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-coalgen-ws/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/probe/run_v025_matrix_probe.py:624)); and
- assignment-identical rows are deduplicated and configuration-ID sorted before the cap check ([lines 656–672](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-coalgen-ws/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/probe/run_v025_matrix_probe.py:656)).

The verifier independently reconstructed this catalogue from the immutable tape plus authenticated stored singleton outcomes. For every anchor, the emitted selected-mapping set exactly equalled the reconstructed set of configurations with `changed_users >= 2`. Inventory:

