## Derived on paper

For a singleton `A={i}`, using its stored default and stored singleton outcome,

`Psi_{ {i} } = Delta F({i}) - d_i = [F(a_i)-F(a^0)] - [F(a_i)-F(a^0)] = 0`.

The executed exact-Fraction test confirms this derivation for all 17,132 catalogue singletons.

At the measured mean, the remaining 158 anchors in the declared 180-anchor order require `158 × 4.614247181818182 = 729.051055` seconds, or `12.151` minutes, of joint-evaluator time only. This is an arithmetic projection, not a total wall-time forecast; it excludes tape construction, reads, context encoding, serialization, and verification.

## Inferred

- The fresh/stored default discrepancy is most plausibly batch-surface numerical dependence because source code, provider digest, archive digest, mapping, field, boundary policy, interpreter, thread pins, and configuration identity were matched, while the dense implementation sorts and chunks the catalogue. No claim is made about which batch surface is globally authoritative; `EVALPATH-2026-09-10.md` remains `UNDETERMINED`.
- Since 93.058% of emitted rows are pairs and only 6.942% represent larger sets, any eventual trained C3 head will be supported mainly on pair interactions. That is a support statement only, not evidence from loss and not evidence about EE.

No learner was trained. Loss values were not used. No EE claim is made.
**The exact source/C3 intersection is 22 anchors; the stated 6,000-label random sample matches the sealed surrogate fallback on 359/6,000 labels (5.9833%); exact-versus-surrogate argmax disagreement is C1 1,137/2,200 (51.6818%), C2 1,216/2,200 (55.2727%), and C3 18/22 (81.8182%); the declared converged run did not launch because the mandated runner rejects its 4,000-update schedule.**

